module acp_goal_demo
  # Goal: the "/goal" idea as a Jet shape -- a persistent, self-verifying loop. You give
  # a goal + a machine-checkable `accept:` condition; each round an agent ATTEMPTS it and
  # a cheap CHECKER decides if the condition is MET, looping with feedback until met or
  # max_rounds. It generalizes Refine (the critic becomes an explicit acceptance gate),
  # and can wrap a sub-shape for each attempt via `via:` (Flow/Architect/Pipeline).
  #
  #   ./jet acp-serve acp_goal_demo::Achiever::handle examples/acp_goal_demo.jet
  #
  # Try: "Implement a fizzbuzz(n) function in Go" -- it will keep going until the build
  # and tests actually pass (the checker reads the command output, not just claims).
  agent Achiever
    runner Goal(drives: "claude-code-acp",
                accept: "The project builds with `go build ./...` and a test passes with `go test ./...`, demonstrated with the actual command output (not just claimed).",
                max_rounds: 5)
    expose handle(goal)
  end
end
